test/check/error-paths.sumspec:12:8:
   |
12 | __path Link = App / Link
   |        ^
path Link has the name of a type; a path's name is new to the spec

test/check/error-paths.sumspec:13:8:
   |
13 | __path P = App
   |        ^
path P has the name of a pattern; a path's name is new to the spec

test/check/error-paths.sumspec:15:8:
   |
15 | __path Q = App
   |        ^
path Q is defined twice (first on line 14)

test/check/error-paths.sumspec:16:8:
   |
16 | __path Loop = Loop
   |        ^
path Loop uses itself; a path may use another, but not in a cycle

test/check/error-paths.sumspec:21:6:
   |
21 | a :: Q -> App(Link.On)
   |      ^
Q is a path, which goes before =>, not where a pattern goes

test/check/error-paths.sumspec:22:6:
   |
22 | b :: P => Link.Off -> Link.On
   |      ^
P is a pattern, which goes where a pattern goes; a shared path is written with paths or a __path

test/check/error-paths.sumspec:23:6:
   |
23 | c :: Bad => Link.Off -> Link.On
   |      ^
Elsewhere is not a variant of Page (in path Bad, at 17:25)

test/check/error-paths.sumspec:24:6:
   |
24 | d :: Loop => Link.Off -> Link.On
   |      ^
path Loop uses itself, so it can't be expanded

